kbase: renew the tiler heap without draining the GPU

Each renewal used to wait for both graphics subqueues on the CPU. Heap
generations are kept until both subqueues have completed a later ring
entry, and each vertex/tiler ring entry stores its heap descriptor into
the subqueue context, so a renewal only swaps descriptors.

